<mujoco model="g1_warehouse_scene">
  <!--
    ==========================================================================
    Agent Mode warehouse scene (TASK-195, place awareness v0)
    ==========================================================================
    The industrial sibling of g1_dex3_room_scene.xml and g1_dex3_house_scene.xml.
    Same robot, same base actuation, same conventions, same include mechanism -
    only the world changed: a 20 x 12 m hall with racking, a loading dock and a
    charging bay instead of an apartment.

      (drawn with '=' and not '-' on purpose: XML forbids a double hyphen inside
      a comment, and an ASCII wall made of them left the house scene unparseable
      by every strict XML tool while MuJoCo's lenient tinyxml accepted it
      happily. Do not "tidy" these back to hyphens.)

    Why an industrial scene at all: place awareness is an industry-first feature
    (placeType is the closed set aisle | rack_face | dock | staging | cell |
    charging | corridor | office | unknown) and there was no industrial scene in
    mjcf/ to resolve places against. This hall exists to test POSE  ->  PLACE
    resolution, not manipulation: everything in it is a static box.

    ======================= PLACE GRAPH GROUND TRUTH ==========================
    The numbers below are the single source of truth. They are transcribed
    verbatim into places/places.warehouse.json; if you move a geom here, move
    the polygon there in the same commit or the resolver silently starts lying.

    Hall bounds (interior, floor 0):  x [-10.0, +10.0]   y [-6.0, +6.0]
    Wall height 4.0 m, wall half thickness 0.05 m centred ON the bound, exactly
    as the house scene does it (so x = +10.0 is the wall centre line and the
    polygons run up to it).

      place id       placeType   footprint (axis aligned unless noted)  keepout
      ============   =========   ====================================  =======
      STAGING        staging     x [-2.0,  2.0]   y [-2.0,  2.0]        no
      AISLE-1        aisle       x [ 2.0,  4.0]   y [-4.0,  2.0]        no
      RACK-A         rack_face   x [ 4.0,  5.0]   y [-4.0,  2.0]        YES
      AISLE-2        aisle       x [ 5.0,  7.0]   y [-4.0,  2.0]        no
      RACK-B         rack_face   x [ 7.0,  8.0]   y [-4.0,  2.0]        YES
      AISLE-3        aisle       x [ 8.0, 10.0]   y [-4.0,  2.0]        no
      DOCK-1         dock        x [-9.0, -5.5]   y [-3.0,  3.0]        no
      DOCK-1-EDGE    dock        x [-9.95,-9.0]   y [-3.0,  3.0]        YES
      CHARGING-A     charging    x [-1.5,  1.5]   y [-5.5, -2.0]        no
      CROSS-AISLE    corridor    L shaped, see below                    no

      CROSS-AISLE polygon, counter clockwise, 6 vertices, concave at (-2, 2):
        (-5.5, -3.0) (-2.0, -3.0) (-2.0, 2.0) (10.0, 2.0) (10.0, 5.5) (-5.5, 5.5)
      i.e. a west leg x [-5.5, -2.0] y [-3.0, 5.5] joined to a north band
      x [-5.5, 10.0] y [2.0, 5.5]. It is deliberately NOT a rectangle: the
      resolver's ray cast has to survive a concave polygon on day one.

    Adjacency the tests lean on (shared edges, never overlaps):
      STAGING  |  AISLE-1      at x = +2.0   (walk +x from spawn)
      STAGING  |  CHARGING-A   at y = -2.0   (walk -y from spawn)
      STAGING  |  CROSS-AISLE  at y = +2.0 and x = -2.0
      aisle mouths             at y = +2.0   (the classic flap location)
      DOCK-1   |  DOCK-1-EDGE  at x = -9.0
    NO two polygons overlap. That is a hard invariant of this scene: a pose
    resolves to at most one place, so the resolver never has to break a tie.

    Uncovered floor is DELIBERATE, not an oversight. y < -4.0 east of staging,
    the pocket x [-3.5, -2.0] y [-6.0, -3.0], the strip north of the dock: a
    pose there is genuinely UNKNOWN and the honesty rule ("null place is never
    silently replaced by the last known place") needs somewhere to be exercised
    that is not a fault injection.

    Floor markings are painted as 4 mm thin boxes with contype = conaffinity = 0
    on the place boundaries, so a render of this scene is a picture of the place
    graph. They sit far below the 0.15 to 1.80 m band the LiDAR cone query uses,
    so they are invisible to range and cannot manufacture a phantom obstacle.
    ==========================================================================

    Robot: g1_dex3/g1_43dof_planarbase.xml, the same generated include the room
    and house scenes use. It spawns at (0, 0) facing world +x, standing in
    STAGING, with three position actuated base DOFs (base_x, base_y, base_yaw,
    slide range +/- 25 m, so the whole hall is reachable). Legs stay in the
    stand pose; there is no gait.

    Unchanged from the room scene and load bearing: PELVIS_Z = 0.807 keeps the
    feet clear of the floor (mj_forward gives ncon = 0 at rest) and sim_node.py's
    weight-0 hold pose must stay LATCHED. Both are covered by e2e_loco_check.py
    checks 2 and 11. Do not "tidy" the pelvis height to make the robot look
    better standing - it ratchets the ankles on the first step.

    World  ->  compass convention, same as the other scenes: +x = 0 deg bearing,
    counter clockwise positive, so +y = +90 deg. base_yaw is the robot heading.
    The place file declares exactly this as "deg,+x=0,CCW+".

    Colour coding follows the house scene's reasoning: a 7B vision model cannot
    tell two grey racks apart but it reliably names "the orange racking" and
    "the yellow roller door", so the landmark colour IS the landmark.

    Sits directly in mjcf/ like the other scenes, so mesh paths of the form
    g1_dex3/meshes/*.STL inside the robot include resolve next to this file.
    Load it exactly like the others, via sim_node.py's scene flag; there is no
    special casing anywhere in the harness for which scene is loaded.
    ==========================================================================
  -->
  <compiler angle="radian" autolimits="true"/>

  <option timestep="0.002" gravity="0 0 -9.81" integrator="implicitfast"/>

  <include file="g1_dex3/g1_43dof_planarbase.xml"/>

  <visual>
    <headlight diffuse="0.55 0.55 0.55" ambient="0.4 0.4 0.4" specular="0.1 0.1 0.1"/>
    <global offwidth="1280" offheight="720"/>
  </visual>

  <asset>
    <texture type="skybox" builtin="gradient" rgb1="0.45 0.55 0.65" rgb2="0.15 0.18 0.22"
             width="512" height="3072"/>
    <texture type="2d" name="whsefloor" builtin="checker" mark="edge"
             rgb1="0.42 0.42 0.43" rgb2="0.35 0.35 0.36" markrgb="0.5 0.5 0.5"
             width="300" height="300"/>
    <material name="whsefloor" texture="whsefloor" texuniform="true"
              texrepeat="20 20" reflectance="0.06"/>

    <material name="wall" rgba="0.80 0.80 0.78 1" specular="0.05" shininess="0.05"/>
    <material name="wall_band" rgba="0.32 0.42 0.52 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>

    <!-- The roller door is the one opening in the shell and the dock landmark. -->
    <material name="door_amber" rgba="0.93 0.72 0.16 1" specular="0.2" shininess="0.2"/>

    <!-- Racking: orange uprights, blue beams. Classic and unmistakable. -->
    <material name="rack_orange" rgba="0.88 0.42 0.10 1" specular="0.2" shininess="0.2"/>
    <material name="rack_blue" rgba="0.13 0.32 0.62 1" specular="0.2" shininess="0.2"/>

    <material name="pallet_wood" rgba="0.68 0.52 0.32 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>
    <material name="box_card" rgba="0.76 0.62 0.42 1" specular="0.05" shininess="0.05"/>
    <material name="box_white" rgba="0.90 0.90 0.88 1" specular="0.05" shininess="0.05"/>
    <material name="steel_grey" rgba="0.72 0.74 0.78 1" specular="0.5" shininess="0.5"/>

    <!-- Charger: green cabinet, the only green thing in the hall. -->
    <material name="charger_green" rgba="0.15 0.62 0.34 1" specular="0.3" shininess="0.3"/>
    <material name="charger_dark" rgba="0.16 0.18 0.20 1" specular="0.2" shininess="0.2"/>

    <!-- Floor paint. mark_red is reserved for keepout footprints. -->
    <material name="mark_yellow" rgba="0.95 0.82 0.15 1" specular="0.0" shininess="0.0"/>
    <material name="mark_blue" rgba="0.20 0.45 0.85 1" specular="0.0" shininess="0.0"/>
    <material name="mark_green" rgba="0.20 0.70 0.35 1" specular="0.0" shininess="0.0"/>
    <material name="mark_red" rgba="0.78 0.16 0.14 1" specular="0.0" shininess="0.0"/>

    <material name="person_shirt" rgba="0.95 0.55 0.10 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>
    <material name="person_skin" rgba="0.90 0.74 0.62 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>
    <material name="person_legs" rgba="0.20 0.22 0.30 1" specular="0.1" shininess="0.1"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- High bay lighting: one directional key plus fills over each functional
         area. A single overhead light leaves the aisles between the 2.2 m racks
         dark enough that the vision model answers "a dark corridor" instead of
         naming the racking. -->
    <light pos="0 0 6.0" dir="0 0 -1" directional="true" diffuse="0.55 0.55 0.55"/>
    <light pos="-7.0 0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.30 0.30 0.30"/>
    <light pos="0 0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.30 0.30 0.30"/>
    <light pos="3.0 -1.0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.32 0.32 0.32"/>
    <light pos="6.0 -1.0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.32 0.32 0.32"/>
    <light pos="9.0 -1.0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.32 0.32 0.32"/>
    <light pos="0 4.0 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.30 0.30 0.30"/>
    <light pos="0 -4.5 4.2" dir="0 0 -1" diffuse="0.28 0.28 0.28"/>

    <geom name="floor" size="0 0 0.05" pos="0 0 0" type="plane" material="whsefloor"
          friction="0.8" condim="3"/>

    <!-- ============== Outer shell: 20 x 12 m, 4.0 m high ==================
         Wall centre lines ARE the hall bounds: +/-10 in x, +/-6 in y. -->
    <geom name="wall_north" type="box" size="10.05 0.05 2.0" pos="0 6 2.0" material="wall"/>
    <geom name="wall_south" type="box" size="10.05 0.05 2.0" pos="0 -6 2.0" material="wall"/>
    <geom name="wall_east"  type="box" size="0.05 6.0 2.0" pos="10 0 2.0" material="wall"/>

    <!-- West end wall, split around the roller door gap y [-1.5, +1.5].
         Segment extents are written as the gap they leave, not as a centre and
         a half size, because it is the GAP that matters. -->
    <geom name="wall_west_a" type="box" size="0.05 2.25 2.0" pos="-10 -3.75 2.0" material="wall"/>
    <geom name="wall_west_b" type="box" size="0.05 2.25 2.0" pos="-10 3.75 2.0" material="wall"/>
    <geom name="wall_west_lintel" type="box" size="0.05 1.50 0.50" pos="-10 0 3.5" material="wall"/>

    <!-- Roller door frame around that gap: the dock landmark. -->
    <geom name="door_roller_l" type="box" size="0.06 0.08 1.50" pos="-9.94 -1.50 1.50"
          material="door_amber"/>
    <geom name="door_roller_r" type="box" size="0.06 0.08 1.50" pos="-9.94 1.50 1.50"
          material="door_amber"/>
    <geom name="door_roller_top" type="box" size="0.06 1.58 0.10" pos="-9.94 0 3.00"
          material="door_amber"/>
    <geom name="door_roller_curtain" type="box" size="0.04 1.50 0.35" pos="-9.90 0 2.65"
          material="door_amber"/>

    <!-- A waist high colour band on the north wall so a head camera pointed at
         a bare 20 m wall still has something to name. -->
    <geom name="wall_band_n" type="box" size="10.0 0.02 0.25" pos="0 5.93 1.30"
          material="wall_band"/>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         RACK-A  x [4.0, 5.0]  y [-4.0, 2.0]   (keepout in the place graph)
         Body origin is the rack centre, (4.5, -1.0). Half sizes: 0.5 x 3.0.
         2.2 m tall, which is inside the LiDAR band, so an aisle wall is a real
         range return and "the aisle is 2 m wide" is measurable, not asserted.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="rack_a" pos="4.5 -1.0 0">
      <geom name="rack_a_post_sw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 -2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_post_se" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 -2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_post_nw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_post_ne" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_post_mw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 0 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_post_me" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 0 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_deck_0" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 0.42"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_deck_1" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.14"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_deck_2" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.86"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_load_0" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.30" pos="0 -2.10 0.75"
            material="box_card"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_load_1" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.30" pos="0 0.40 0.75"
            material="box_white"/>
      <geom name="rack_a_load_2" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.28" pos="0 2.05 1.45"
            material="box_card"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         RACK-B  x [7.0, 8.0]  y [-4.0, 2.0]   (keepout in the place graph)
         Centre (7.5, -1.0). Identical geometry to RACK-A on purpose: two
         same shaped places 3 m apart is exactly the situation a place resolver
         with no hysteresis gets wrong.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="rack_b" pos="7.5 -1.0 0">
      <geom name="rack_b_post_sw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 -2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_post_se" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 -2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_post_nw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_post_ne" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_post_mw" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="-0.44 0 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_post_me" type="box" size="0.06 0.06 1.10" pos="0.44 0 1.10"
            material="rack_orange" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_deck_0" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 0.42"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_deck_1" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.14"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_deck_2" type="box" size="0.50 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.86"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_load_0" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.30" pos="0 -1.55 0.75"
            material="box_white"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_load_1" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.30" pos="0 1.20 0.75"
            material="box_card"/>
      <geom name="rack_b_load_2" type="box" size="0.38 0.52 0.28" pos="0 -0.30 1.45"
            material="box_white"/>
    </body>

    <!-- AISLE-3's east flank is the hall wall itself: a fourth free standing
         rack row would have to eat into the 2.0 m the spec fixes for an aisle.
         Shallow wall shelving (0.10 m deep, x [9.85, 9.95]) makes the aisle read
         as an aisle from the head camera at the cost of 0.10 m of free width.
         It stands INSIDE the AISLE-3 polygon on purpose: the place graph
         describes the surveyed bay, not the swept free space, exactly like the
         racking that lines a real aisle. -->
    <body name="rack_c_wall" pos="9.90 -1.0 0">
      <geom name="rack_c_deck_0" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 0.42"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_c_deck_1" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.14"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_c_deck_2" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.03" pos="0 0 1.86"
            material="rack_blue" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="rack_c_post_s" type="box" size="0.05 0.06 1.10" pos="0 -2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange"/>
      <geom name="rack_c_post_n" type="box" size="0.05 0.06 1.10" pos="0 2.94 1.10"
            material="rack_orange"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         DOCK-1  x [-9.0, -5.5]  y [-3.0, 3.0]
         The loading dock behind the roller door. Pallets staged inside the
         place, none of them across the DOCK-1-EDGE keepout line at x = -9.0.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="dock_pallet_a" pos="-8.20 -2.10 0">
      <geom name="dock_pallet_a_base" type="box" size="0.60 0.40 0.07" pos="0 0 0.07"
            material="pallet_wood" friction="0.7" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="dock_pallet_a_load" type="box" size="0.54 0.36 0.34" pos="0 0 0.48"
            material="box_card" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
    </body>

    <body name="dock_pallet_b" pos="-6.60 1.90 0">
      <geom name="dock_pallet_b_base" type="box" size="0.60 0.40 0.07" pos="0 0 0.07"
            material="pallet_wood" friction="0.7" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="dock_pallet_b_load" type="box" size="0.52 0.34 0.46" pos="0 0 0.60"
            material="box_white" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
    </body>

    <!-- Dock office kiosk against the south side of the dock. Gives DOCK-1 a
         landmark that is not a pallet, and gives the "office" placeType a real
         world referent for whoever extends this graph later. -->
    <body name="dock_kiosk" pos="-6.25 -2.50 0">
      <geom name="dock_kiosk_body" type="box" size="0.60 0.42 0.90" pos="0 0 0.90"
            material="steel_grey" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="dock_kiosk_window" type="box" size="0.50 0.02 0.30" pos="0 0.44 1.40"
            material="wall_band"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         CHARGING-A  x [-1.5, 1.5]  y [-5.5, -2.0]
         A marked bay off the south edge of STAGING. The charger cabinet stands
         against the south wall, fully inside the bay.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="charger" pos="0 -5.15 0">
      <geom name="charger_cabinet" type="box" size="0.55 0.30 0.75" pos="0 0 0.75"
            material="charger_green" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="charger_head" type="box" size="0.55 0.32 0.10" pos="0 0 1.60"
            material="charger_dark"/>
      <geom name="charger_pillar_l" type="box" size="0.07 0.07 0.40" pos="-0.48 0.34 0.40"
            material="charger_dark"/>
      <geom name="charger_pillar_r" type="box" size="0.07 0.07 0.40" pos="0.48 0.34 0.40"
            material="charger_dark"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         STAGING  x [-2.0, 2.0]  y [-2.0, 2.0]   robot spawns at (0, 0)
         Kept deliberately clear around the spawn: one pallet in the north west
         corner so the very first head camera frame is not an empty floor, and
         nothing within 1.2 m of the origin.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="staging_pallet" pos="-1.55 1.50 0">
      <geom name="staging_pallet_base" type="box" size="0.42 0.42 0.07" pos="0 0 0.07"
            material="pallet_wood" friction="0.7" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="staging_pallet_load" type="box" size="0.36 0.36 0.30" pos="0 0 0.44"
            material="box_card" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         CROSS-AISLE furniture. A single steel column at the concave corner of
         the L, so the one place whose polygon is not a rectangle also has a
         landmark exactly where the geometry is interesting.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="cross_column" pos="-2.60 2.60 0">
      <geom name="cross_column_post" type="box" size="0.14 0.14 1.75" pos="0 0 1.75"
            material="steel_grey" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
      <geom name="cross_column_guard" type="box" size="0.22 0.22 0.28" pos="0 0 0.28"
            material="mark_yellow" friction="0.6" condim="3"/>
    </body>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         Floor paint: the place graph, drawn. 4 mm slabs, collision off, well
         below the 0.15 to 1.80 m LiDAR band so they never become an obstacle.
         Every stripe below sits ON a boundary listed in the header table.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <!-- STAGING outline, blue. The south stripe is shared with CHARGING-A's
         north edge and the north stripe with CROSS-AISLE's south edge, which
         is why neither of those places repaints it. -->
    <geom name="mark_staging_n" type="box" size="2.00 0.05 0.002" pos="0 2.0 0.002"
          material="mark_blue" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_staging_s" type="box" size="2.00 0.05 0.002" pos="0 -2.0 0.002"
          material="mark_blue" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_staging_w" type="box" size="0.05 2.00 0.002" pos="-2.0 0 0.002"
          material="mark_blue" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_staging_e" type="box" size="0.05 2.00 0.002" pos="2.0 0 0.002"
          material="mark_blue" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- Aisle mouths at y = +2.0, yellow. These three lines are where a naive
         resolver flaps, so they are painted and therefore checkable on camera. -->
    <geom name="mark_aisle1_mouth" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="3.0 2.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_aisle2_mouth" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="6.0 2.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_aisle3_mouth" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="9.0 2.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <!-- Aisle south ends at y = -4.0. -->
    <geom name="mark_aisle1_end" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="3.0 -4.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_aisle2_end" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="6.0 -4.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_aisle3_end" type="box" size="1.00 0.05 0.002" pos="9.0 -4.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- CHARGING-A bay, green. North edge omitted: it is the STAGING stripe. -->
    <geom name="mark_charge_w" type="box" size="0.05 1.75 0.002" pos="-1.5 -3.75 0.002"
          material="mark_green" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_charge_e" type="box" size="0.05 1.75 0.002" pos="1.5 -3.75 0.002"
          material="mark_green" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_charge_s" type="box" size="1.50 0.05 0.002" pos="0 -5.5 0.002"
          material="mark_green" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- DOCK-1 outline, yellow. Its east edge is NOT painted here: x = -5.5 is
         shared with CROSS-AISLE's west leg and is painted once, below. Two
         coincident 4 mm slabs on the same line z fight in every renderer. -->
    <geom name="mark_dock_n" type="box" size="1.75 0.05 0.002" pos="-7.25 3.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_dock_s" type="box" size="1.75 0.05 0.002" pos="-7.25 -3.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- DOCK-1-EDGE keepout, red, filled rather than outlined: it is the strip
         a truck tail lift swings into and the robot must never stand in. -->
    <geom name="mark_dock_edge" type="box" size="0.475 3.00 0.002" pos="-9.475 0 0.002"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_dock_edge_line" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.003" pos="-9.0 0 0.003"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- RACK-A / RACK-B keepout footprints, red outline on the aisle facing
         sides so the painted floor and the place graph agree. -->
    <geom name="mark_rack_a_w" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.002" pos="4.0 -1.0 0.002"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_rack_a_e" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.002" pos="5.0 -1.0 0.002"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_rack_b_w" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.002" pos="7.0 -1.0 0.002"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_rack_b_e" type="box" size="0.05 3.00 0.002" pos="8.0 -1.0 0.002"
          material="mark_red" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- CROSS-AISLE: only the two edges that are not shared with another place
         (the west leg's west and south edges) plus the north band's north edge. -->
    <geom name="mark_cross_leg_w" type="box" size="0.05 4.25 0.002" pos="-5.5 1.25 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_cross_leg_s" type="box" size="1.75 0.05 0.002" pos="-3.75 -3.0 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    <geom name="mark_cross_band_n" type="box" size="7.75 0.05 0.002" pos="2.25 5.5 0.002"
          material="mark_yellow" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         Person figure, on the dock.
         A crude standing figure, not a person model: the idle watcher only ever
         asks the VLM "is a person in the image?" - no faces, no identities,
         nothing to recognise. Mocap body so a test can teleport it in and out
         of view; collision off so it can never trip the robot. High vis orange
         torso, because that is what a person on a dock wears.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <body name="person" pos="-7.40 0.90 0" mocap="true">
      <geom name="person_leg_l" type="capsule" size="0.055" fromto="0.0 0.09 0.03 0.0 0.09 0.82"
            material="person_legs" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <geom name="person_leg_r" type="capsule" size="0.055" fromto="0.0 -0.09 0.03 0.0 -0.09 0.82"
            material="person_legs" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <geom name="person_torso" type="capsule" size="0.145" fromto="0 0 0.85 0 0 1.34"
            material="person_shirt" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <geom name="person_arm_l" type="capsule" size="0.045" fromto="0 0.17 1.30 0 0.21 0.88"
            material="person_shirt" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <geom name="person_arm_r" type="capsule" size="0.045" fromto="0 -0.17 1.30 0 -0.21 0.88"
            material="person_shirt" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <geom name="person_head" type="sphere" size="0.105" pos="0 0 1.48"
            material="person_skin" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    </body>

    <!-- Debug / recording cameras. The agent never uses any of them: it only
         ever reads the head camera on the robot itself. The overview is framed
         so the painted place graph is legible end to end, because "does the
         robot think it is where the paint says it is" is the whole task. -->
    <camera name="warehouse_overview" pos="0 0 20.0" xyaxes="1 0 0 0 1 0" fovy="38"/>
    <camera name="warehouse_iso" pos="-16.0 -14.0 12.0"
            xyaxes="0.659 -0.753 0 0.370 0.324 0.871" fovy="34"/>
    <!-- Follows the robot from a fixed perch south of the hall: targetbody keeps
         the position and re aims at the pelvis, so one camera works in every
         place instead of needing one per place. The perch height is not a taste
         decision: the sightline to a robot at the origin crosses the y = -6 wall
         at z = 7.5 m, clear of its 4.0 m top, and clears the 2.2 m racking from
         every aisle. -->
    <camera name="warehouse_follow" mode="targetbody" target="pelvis" pos="0 -12.0 14.0"
            fovy="22"/>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
